                            <comment id="503615" author="adilger" created="Wed, 14 Oct 2026 11:51:36 +0000">&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class="error"&gt;&amp;#91;Claude&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt; Also seen with the OST unmounted rather than failing bulk reads (see the &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20212" title="FLR-ECRO: verify non-write RPCs do not block client " class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20212"&gt;LU-20212&lt;/a&gt; test results): an mmap read of a 4+2 EC file in RDONLY state, and &lt;tt&gt;git status&lt;/tt&gt;/&lt;tt&gt;git grep&lt;/tt&gt; on a git tree stored with an EC default layout, blocked for the whole outage (60s and 300s) while &lt;tt&gt;read()&lt;/tt&gt; of the same files was rebuilt from parity in under 1s.  The faulting tasks wait in the OST lock enqueue, and the glimpse from &lt;tt&gt;vvp_prep_size()&lt;/tt&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;osc_lock_enqueue &amp;lt; cl_lock_enqueue &amp;lt; lov_lock_enqueue &amp;lt; cl_lock_enqueue &amp;lt; cl_lock_request &amp;lt; cl_io_lock &amp;lt; cl_io_loop &amp;lt; __ll_fault &amp;lt; ll_fault &amp;lt; __do_fault
cl_sync_io_wait &amp;lt; cl_lock_request &amp;lt; cl_glimpse_lock &amp;lt; vvp_prep_size &amp;lt; vvp_io_fault_start &amp;lt; cl_io_start &amp;lt; cl_io_loop &amp;lt; __ll_fault &amp;lt; ll_fault
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;CIT_FAULT never sets &lt;tt&gt;ci_ndelay&lt;/tt&gt;, so it neither fails over nor switches to CIT_EC_RD.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
